Hi @hnyls2002 @hzh0425 — sorry for the direct ping; you two seem to handle `run-ci` labels most often lately.

Three small MiMo-V2.5 fixes are currently blocked only by the label gate (all red checks are the `pr-gate` label check itself; the 90 real test jobs are skipped):

- #37060 (this one): one-line fix for a scheduler deadlock when serving MiMo-V2.5 with `--tp 8 --dp 2 --enable-dp-attention` and any audio input — full analysis in #37059, verified on 8×H200 (fp8 + bf16, 12/12 multimodal cases, plus an independent second verification round in the comments);
- #37063: retry for the `freeze_gc` startup race under `--skip-server-warmup`;
- #37064: warning when `--dtype auto` silently falls back to fp16 for configs with no declared torch_dtype.

Could you add `run-ci` so CI can actually run? Happy to rebase or address any review feedback. Thanks!

